    The code generator keeps the static parameters in scope, and binds a typecase tuple pattern's names

    Climb batch 33, rung V (rows 812 and 822). The code generator read a
    type's inherited methods, and compiled a generic function's or method's
    body, with none of the static parameters in scope in its kind
    environment, so a generic trait that defines a member of a trait whose
    comprises clause lists a type at a where-clause variable stopped, 'E is
    not in the kind env', where the checker passes it. It now reads them
    with the type's static parameters and where clause, compiles a generic
    body with its own, and binds each name of a typecase clause's tuple
    pattern to its element, through which row 822's crash came (row 1066).
    The one library's ArrayList and APPCOV pass this wall. Rows 1066 to
    1068 are new; F-384 is new, F-181 and F-281 rewritten.

