    The compiled code casts self at a conditional's arm and a closure's result, and loads no class to choose an opcode

    Climb batch 33, rung Q (rows 1051, 1050 and 1052). In a self-typed trait
    or a trait with a comprises clause the checker types self as the trait
    met with the implementing type, but the code generator cast no arm of a
    conditional and no function expression's or local function's result, so
    each failed the JVM's verification when its class loaded; the one
    library's StandardTotalOrder has the first form in MIN, MAX and MINMAX.
    Each arm and each closure's result is now cast where its static type is
    not already below the declared type, as rung K casts a method's returned
    value. The class loader chose a call's opcode by loading the owner class,
    which died with ClassCircularityError where an object lists a self-typed
    trait first; it now reads the owner's class file. Rows 1069 to 1071 are
    new; F-385 is new, F-377 and F-225 rewritten; Appendix I's sentence on
    the closure and the conditional at the self parameter says that they run.

    This commit edits the original tree.
