    Skeptic's fix: a getter on an intersection goes to a conjunct whose method of its name takes no argument

    Edits the original tree. Where a dotted call on a receiver typed by an
    intersection has no arrow, as a desugared getter's, the owner among the
    conjuncts was any conjunct with a method of the call's name. A getter of one
    conjunct beside a method of its name with a parameter in the other compiled
    to a call of the other's absent getter and died with NoSuchMethodError, the
    conjuncts in either order (walk: 'sided flagged 3'). Now only the conjuncts
    with a method of the name that takes the call's argument by its number of
    parameters qualify (CodeGen.takesArgumentOf); fork I1 asks for the conjunct
    that declares or inherits the called method. TypecaseBinderMethodCall
    asserts both orders.

